# Agency Compatibility Preview Release

Status: DONE
Milestone: Public unsigned Windows11 x64 v0.2.0-preview.3 / Windows0.2.0.3
Dependencies: 58_INSTALLER_RELEASE.todo, 62_PUBLIC_PREVIEW_RELEASE.todo, 63_AGENCY_VERSION_COMPATIBILITY.todo

## Purpose

Publish the completed disabled-Ask repair and backward/forward runtime-contract compatibility
through the existing unsigned preview channel. The owner requested publication on October11
at20:29. This is not a claim that every device, capture backend or future provider is qualified.

## Tasks

- [x] Confirm publication request and existing repository-scoped publishing access.
- [x] Update candidate version, current guides, website links and reviewed source annotations.
- [x] Freeze full source-matched handbook/atlas editions and commit all candidate inputs.
- [x] Build Setup/Portable from that clean commit using existing offline runtime/compiler.
- [x] Verify exact payload/archive inventories, native dependencies, generated PCM and clean exits.
- [x] Exercise exact packaged synthetic UI, launcher checks and isolated installer lifecycle.
- [x] Attach exact committed PDFs and verify checksums; keep prior releases immutable.
- [x] Publish the new tagged public prerelease and verify all five downloadable assets.
- [x] Record exact publication/qualification evidence and push the release source; maintain separate follow-up editions.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] New assets contain workstream63's repair and match their clean source/tag identity.
- [x] Existing application/provider settings are not reset; no real recording, login or model call
  is needed merely to package the already-exercised fix.
- [x] Synthetic/current-host evidence is separate from clean-VM, genuine old-binary migration,
  owner comfort, real-meeting recognition and recipient-capture qualification.
- [x] Preview1/2 tags and assets are unchanged; published books match the exact packaged commit.
- [x] No automatic fallback or relaxed safety contract is introduced by release packaging.

